# Git Commit Rules

Apply whenever creating or drafting git commits.

## Forbidden Trailers

- Never add `Co-authored-by:` trailers to commit messages.
- Never add AI attribution, generated-by notices, or similar trailers (e.g. `Generated-by:`, `Signed-off-by:` for AI, model names).

## Message Style

- Concise, imperative mood, describing the actual change.
- Prefer Conventional Commits when they fit:

```text
feat: add canonical transaction type
refactor: introduce global state store
test: update cryptography tests for unified signature API
docs: add domain model ownership ADR
```

## Examples

```text
# ✅ GOOD
feat: add canonical transaction type
fix: reject duplicate mempool entries by tx id

# ❌ BAD
Updated stuff and also fixed things
feat: add transaction type

Co-authored-by: Some AI <ai@example.com>
```
